1
00:00:07,929 --> 00:00:13,203
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,359 --> 00:00:15,371
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:21,017 --> 00:00:22,887
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:22,928 --> 00:00:26,712
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

5
00:00:27,324 --> 00:00:29,891
We're carrying on with lessons from Uhud(أحَد).

6
00:00:30,824 --> 00:00:36,019
Why were youth such as Rafiyah Bin Khateej(رافع بن خديج) and Samurah Bin Jundub(سَمُرَةْ بن جندب)

7
00:00:36,112 --> 00:00:39,789
and some others like Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) and Al-Bara'a Bin Aazib(البراء بن عازب),

8
00:00:40,712 --> 00:00:42,535
why were they so eager to join the fight.

9
00:00:43,415 --> 00:00:49,283
One might argue that the reason is that they belong to a militant society.

10
00:00:49,323 --> 00:00:51,186
I mean, one could say that,

11
00:00:51,497 --> 00:00:55,359
well that was the lifestyle of the Arabs, this was a warlike people,

12
00:00:55,902 --> 00:00:57,886
all what they did was fight, fight, fight.

13
00:00:58,463 --> 00:01:04,012
So it's not really strange that these kids would want to join in war and battle

14
00:01:04,052 --> 00:01:07,703
 because that's part of being a man in Arabia.

15
00:01:07,783 --> 00:01:11,021
When one could argue from this point of view.

16
00:01:11,695 --> 00:01:17,314
But one could respond back by saying that, that's not necessarily the case.

17
00:01:17,814 --> 00:01:23,212
 Because when youngsters such as Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر), Al-Bara'a Bin Aazib(البرآء بن عازب)

18
00:01:23,448 --> 00:01:26,138
Samoorah(سَمُرَةْ) and Rafiah(رافع) wanted to join the army,

19
00:01:26,374 --> 00:01:29,251
on the other hand, we have about 300, who defected.

20
00:01:30,145 --> 00:01:35,434
So, it's not all about the society and this being a society of warriors that's not really true.

21
00:01:35,938 --> 00:01:37,964
The issue here is Eeman(ايمان),

22
00:01:38,391 --> 00:01:40,980
the ones who had Eeman(ايمان) and the ones who didn't have it

23
00:01:41,308 --> 00:01:44,067
the ones who had Eeman(ايمان) would so eager to join

24
00:01:44,276 --> 00:01:47,968
and the ones who didn't have it was so eager to run away.

25
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:53,598
Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن اُبَيئ) and 300 of his men defected, in the day of Uhud(أحَد),

26
00:01:54,042 --> 00:01:56,801
 withdrew, they refuse to fight.

27
00:01:57,289 --> 00:01:59,415
And this was the case in many of the other battles,

28
00:01:59,455 --> 00:02:03,479
 they refused to join in Tabook(تبوك), they refused to join in Al-Khandaq(الخندق).

29
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:06,813
 So, they run away in times of fear.

30
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:10,464
And I use the word defected a lot.

31
00:02:10,544 --> 00:02:14,892
And again, probably in one sense, this is the right word to use,

32
00:02:14,932 --> 00:02:18,816
because them withdrawing is really them being on the side of the enemy.

33
00:02:19,098 --> 00:02:22,479
But I don't want it to be understood that they defected to the enemy side,

34
00:02:22,519 --> 00:02:23,274
 that's not the case,

35
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:27,192
I mean, they withdrew back to Uhud(أحَد), they didn't go and fight to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

36
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:31,605
 But even though they weren't participating in the fight, but one can say that

37
00:02:32,045 --> 00:02:33,884
they were part of the enemy's army

38
00:02:33,924 --> 00:02:38,130
 because they would support them with information, they would act as spies for them.

39
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:41,695
So, don't take the word literal, it does have a correct meaning,

40
00:02:41,735 --> 00:02:42,886
but not in a literal sense.

41
00:02:43,425 --> 00:02:47,064
It's not that they actually physically defected to the enemy's army.

42
00:02:48,235 --> 00:02:53,913
Next lesson one can see one of the characteristics of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) in this battle.

43
00:02:54,407 --> 00:02:56,781
They refused to fight in Uhud(أحَد), because of fear of death.

44
00:02:57,011 --> 00:02:58,450
When Rasool Allah ﷺ came back,

45
00:02:59,731 --> 00:03:03,107
and he wanted to pursue Abu Sufiyaan(ابوسفيان),

46
00:03:03,422 --> 00:03:05,825
in what is referred to Ghazwa Hamra'a Al-Asad(غزوة حمراء الاسد).

47
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:08,525
The Munafiqeen(منافقين) in this time wanted to join

48
00:03:09,276 --> 00:03:11,476
but Rasool Allah ﷺ this time refused to allow them to join.

49
00:03:11,516 --> 00:03:14,043
 He said only the ones who joined me in Uhud(أحَد), can join me now.

50
00:03:15,041 --> 00:03:17,640
And why did they want to join in Hamra Al-Asad(حمراء الاسد), because

51
00:03:18,204 --> 00:03:20,238
they thought there is a good possibility of winning.

52
00:03:20,278 --> 00:03:24,797
 So, there could be some booties of war, to get some of those spoils.

53
00:03:25,129 --> 00:03:28,093
So, this is a characteristic of Munafiqeen(منافقين),

54
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:31,607
they want to take the worldly benefits from Islam,

55
00:03:32,532 --> 00:03:36,548
but they refuse to pay the demands of Islam.

56
00:03:37,485 --> 00:03:40,767
They want the gains, but they don't want the pains.

57
00:03:41,585 --> 00:03:44,523
They want Ghanimah(غنيمه), but they don't want to fight.

58
00:03:45,335 --> 00:03:49,450
 So, this mindset of being a Muslim when it's convenient

59
00:03:49,794 --> 00:03:53,242
and giving it up, when I'm demanded sacrifice

60
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:56,159
is a sign of hypocrisy.

61
00:03:56,324 --> 00:03:59,038
And it applies to many situations,

62
00:03:59,481 --> 00:04:00,486
and it's very dangerous,

63
00:04:00,526 --> 00:04:05,102
and one should try to check up, themselves and see if that's the case

64
00:04:05,479 --> 00:04:09,728
do I become enthusiastic to join in Islamic activities

65
00:04:09,768 --> 00:04:12,639
 when I feel that there's a worldly benefit for me, in it

66
00:04:12,992 --> 00:04:16,195
but when it becomes demanding then I give it up.

67
00:04:17,104 --> 00:04:18,008
For example,

68
00:04:18,366 --> 00:04:24,511
you might know some parents, who are very happy about Islam,

69
00:04:24,551 --> 00:04:29,815
when it comes to the part of Islam that talks about children being obedient to their parents

70
00:04:29,905 --> 00:04:34,784
and respecting their parents and the rights of the parents being second to Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

71
00:04:35,009 --> 00:04:38,738
and all of those Aayaat(آيات) in Qur'an and Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

72
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:41,368
that tell them to take care of their moms and dads

73
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:42,998
so they love that part of Islam.

74
00:04:43,327 --> 00:04:48,871
However, when it comes to the part of Islam that tells their son to go and for example, fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عَزّوجَلّ),

75
00:04:49,217 --> 00:04:52,664
No, they don't want that part and they don't want their children to hear about that part.

76
00:04:53,336 --> 00:04:56,769
 So, I love Islam, when it's gonna tell my sons to be submissive,

77
00:04:57,521 --> 00:05:00,395
but I don't like it when it tells them to go and give up their lives.

78
00:05:01,219 --> 00:05:05,818
Or, for example, the husband who loves the Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

79
00:05:05,858 --> 00:05:09,048
He said; If I was going to tell a woman to make Sujood(سجود) to anyone other than Allah,

80
00:05:09,088 --> 00:05:11,791
then I would tell her, to make Sujood(سجود) to her husband.

81
00:05:12,628 --> 00:05:15,944
And if the husband goes to bed and he's upset with his wife,

82
00:05:16,055 --> 00:05:19,054
then the angels will curse the wife until the morning

83
00:05:19,463 --> 00:05:21,402
and he would repeat all of those Ahadith(احاديث).

84
00:05:21,577 --> 00:05:25,761
But when it comes to the Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, being kind to his wives

85
00:05:26,075 --> 00:05:29,228
when it comes to the stories of the Sahabah(صحابه) being kind to their wives

86
00:05:29,482 --> 00:05:31,078
he wants to hide those away.

87
00:05:31,897 --> 00:05:36,721
Some scholars, for example, they love to talk about how you should respect the scholar

88
00:05:36,761 --> 00:05:40,408
 and how you should obey the scholar and listen to their fatwah(فتوى)

89
00:05:40,551 --> 00:05:43,744
and not disagree with them, and you should honor them.

90
00:05:44,315 --> 00:05:49,776
 But then the scholar would shy away from the parts of Islam that tell them that they need to speak the truth,

91
00:05:50,117 --> 00:05:51,468
 they need to speak the whole truth,

92
00:05:51,713 --> 00:05:53,001
they should hide nothing from it

93
00:05:53,181 --> 00:05:58,689
and they should speak the truth even if they're going to have to pay the price with, their own lives.

94
00:05:59,852 --> 00:06:05,394
So this duality, of wanting to be a Muslim, when it's convenient

95
00:06:05,828 --> 00:06:09,766
and trying to cover up the other parts is not a good thing.

96
00:06:10,318 --> 00:06:13,444
And as we see here, its the sign of Nifaaq(نفاق), so one needs to be careful

97
00:06:13,804 --> 00:06:17,160
and make sure that they don't belong to this category of people.

98
00:06:17,612 --> 00:06:20,207
ادخُلُوا فِي السِّلمِ كَافَّةً

99
00:06:20,553 --> 00:06:24,615
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, you take Islam in its entirety.

100
00:06:25,104 --> 00:06:29,745
You don't take some parts and leave others that's the sign of the People of the Book.

101
00:06:30,355 --> 00:06:33,147
They believed in, part of the book and they rejected others,

102
00:06:34,485 --> 00:06:36,407
so we have to accept it all.

103
00:06:36,705 --> 00:06:40,293
And Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he took Baiyah(بيعة) from Al-Ansaar(الانصار) the Baiyah(بيعة) was

104
00:06:40,653 --> 00:06:43,134
اَطَّاعَهْ فِيْ الْمَنْشَط وَالْمَكرَهْ

105
00:06:43,449 --> 00:06:46,932
You obey me in times of ease and in times of difficulty.

106
00:06:48,213 --> 00:06:51,736
It's not when you like it, and then you neglect it when you don't.

107
00:06:52,441 --> 00:06:54,979
You have to take the whole package, as it is.

108
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:57,552
Next lesson, Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن قيم) says;

109
00:06:58,155 --> 00:07:00,099
that one of the benefits of Uhud(أحَد) is

110
00:07:00,558 --> 00:07:05,279
اِسْتِخْرَاجُ عُبُوْدِيَّة اُوْلِيَآءِهِ وَحِزْبِهِ فِي السَّرَّآءِ وَ الضرَّآءْ

111
00:07:05,954 --> 00:07:11,173
فَاِذَا ثَبَتُ عَلَى الطَّاعَتِ وَالْعُبُوْدِيَّةْ فِيْمَا يُحِبُّوْنَ وَ يَكْرَهُوْنْ فَمْ عَبِيْدُوْ حَقًا

112
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:16,165
وَلَيْسُ كَمَنْ يَعَبْدُاللهَ عَلَى حَرْفٍ وَاحِدْ مِنَّ السَّرَّآءِ وَنْعْمَ وَالْعَافِيَّه فَقَطْ

113
00:07:17,239 --> 00:07:23,104
So, one of the lessons of Uhud(أحَد) is to show the servitude of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

114
00:07:23,682 --> 00:07:28,400
that they are willing to worship Allahعَزّوجَلّ in times of ease and in times of difficulty.

115
00:07:28,749 --> 00:07:32,954
So, if they are firm and steadfast on the religion on both situations,

116
00:07:33,297 --> 00:07:36,302
that's a sign of true servitude, Uboodiyah (عبودية).

117
00:07:37,164 --> 00:07:42,785
And that's unlike people who only worship Allahعَزّوجَلّ on one condition,

118
00:07:43,206 --> 00:07:46,150
 you know, they're program to only worship Allah, if things are tough

119
00:07:46,442 --> 00:07:48,719
they only program to worship Allah, if things are easy,

120
00:07:49,247 --> 00:07:51,564
but they don't have the combination of both.

121
00:07:52,513 --> 00:07:55,813
So, sometimes people only remember Allahعَزّوجَلّ when things get tough

122
00:07:56,305 --> 00:07:58,660
then they start making Dua(دُعَا), O Allah,

123
00:07:58,827 --> 00:08:01,668
 for example all of those Bachelors out there.

124
00:08:02,147 --> 00:08:06,410
They're making Dua(دعا) in every Salah(صلاة), in every Sujood(سجود) O Allah, I want to get married,

125
00:08:07,095 --> 00:08:09,299
they would pray Qayyam Ul-Lail(قيام اليل),

126
00:08:09,526 --> 00:08:12,004
they would make this Dua(دعا) between Azaan(اذان) and Iqaamah(اقامه),

127
00:08:12,257 --> 00:08:14,465
they would make this Dua(دعا), when they're making Eitkaaf(اعتكاف),

128
00:08:14,777 --> 00:08:17,130
they would do it on the night of the 27th.

129
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:18,875
O Allah I want to get married.

130
00:08:19,317 --> 00:08:21,669
And as soon as they get married, they stop making Dua(دعا).

131
00:08:22,504 --> 00:08:26,310
So, that's an example of somebody who only worships Allahعَزّوجَلّ when things are difficult,

132
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:28,935
 but when things get easy, they forget about Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

133
00:08:29,806 --> 00:08:33,820
Like the story Allah mentions in Qur'an, of the people who are in the middle of the sea

134
00:08:34,154 --> 00:08:36,805
and the storm picks up and they feel that they're going to die

135
00:08:36,864 --> 00:08:42,158
and there's no one to ask except Allahعَزّوجَلّ you're in the middle of nowhere, you're in the middle of the ocean.

136
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:44,566
Your only refuge is Allahعَزّوجَلّ

137
00:08:44,606 --> 00:08:48,175
so they make Dua(دعا) to Allahعَزّوجَلّ they don't make Dua(دعا) to their idols false gods,

138
00:08:48,255 --> 00:08:49,351
 they make Dua(دعا) to Allah.

139
00:08:49,913 --> 00:08:51,786
And when Allah delivers them to safety,

140
00:08:52,076 --> 00:08:56,063
then they go back and make Sujood(سجود) to their idols, he also says;

141
00:08:56,409 --> 00:08:59,300
اِنَّه’ اِذَا امتَحَنَهُمْ بِالْغَلَبَة وَالْكَثْرَةْ

142
00:08:59,739 --> 00:09:02,200
وَالْهزِيْمَهْ ذَلُّوْا وَ انكَسرُوْا وَخَضعوا

143
00:09:02,661 --> 00:09:04,592
فَاسْتَوْجَبُوْا مِنْه’ الْعِزَّةْ وَالْنَصْر

144
00:09:04,923 --> 00:09:08,671
فَاِنَّ خُلْعَةً النَّصْرِ اِنَّمَا تَكُوْنُ مَعَ ولاية الذل وَالْاِنْكِسَارْ

145
00:09:09,218 --> 00:09:16,297
He said, that Allahعَزّوجَلّ tested them by them being defeated, and humiliated.

146
00:09:16,631 --> 00:09:24,747
And weaken so that made them humble themselves in front of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

147
00:09:24,787 --> 00:09:27,333
 and humiliate themselves in front of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

148
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:31,071
And that is when Allahعَزّوجَلّ responds to your Dua(دعا),

149
00:09:31,111 --> 00:09:34,938
when you humble yourself in front of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

150
00:09:35,496 --> 00:09:41,540
and you show Him true servitude that is when Allahعَزّوجَلّ responds to your Dua(دعا).

151
00:09:42,254 --> 00:09:43,841
 So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ said about Badr(بدر);

152
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:47,349
وَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ بِبَدْرٍ وَأَنْتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ ۖ

153
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:51,872
Allahعَزّوجَلّ gave you victory in Badr(بدر), when you were weak

154
00:09:52,923 --> 00:09:54,061
While in Hunain(حنين)

155
00:09:54,121 --> 00:09:57,613
وَيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ إِذْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ فَلَمْ تُغْنِ عَنْكُمْ شَيْئًا

156
00:09:57,831 --> 00:10:01,563
While in Hunain(حنين) because you are dependent on your numbers you lost.

157
00:10:03,258 --> 00:10:04,385
He also says,

158
00:10:04,528 --> 00:10:08,020
and this will be our last lesson that we talked about in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد)

159
00:10:08,299 --> 00:10:12,455
اِنَّ وَقْعَتْ اُحَدْ كَانَتْ مُقَدِّمَهْ وَيَرْحَاسًا بَيْنَ يَدَيْه مَوْتْ رَسُوْل الله

160
00:10:12,730 --> 00:10:22,254
Uhud(أحَد), was a preparation for the most catastrophic event that will ever happen to the Muslims.

161
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:27,593
Because this event is so great, they needed to be prepared for it.

162
00:10:29,072 --> 00:10:31,844
And that is the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ

163
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:38,579
and since Rasool Allah ﷺ was everything for Sahabah(صحابه) in terms of Islam.

164
00:10:39,067 --> 00:10:42,149
You know, they learned Islam from him, he was their source.

165
00:10:42,244 --> 00:10:43,885
They didn't have any books to go and consult.

166
00:10:43,925 --> 00:10:46,930
They didn't have any scholars to go and talk to, they didn't have any Jama'at(جماعات)

167
00:10:47,310 --> 00:10:49,581
to recruit them and teach them about Islam.

168
00:10:49,822 --> 00:10:53,657
Rasool Allah ﷺ was their source and their only source.

169
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:58,509
So, he was their father, he was everything for them.

170
00:10:59,254 --> 00:11:01,929
So, for them to lose him is not gonna be an easy thing

171
00:11:02,418 --> 00:11:12,245
it's going to be a huge setback and it will cause a serious psychological affect on the hearts of the Muslims,

172
00:11:12,325 --> 00:11:13,760
 so they need to be prepared for that.

173
00:11:14,405 --> 00:11:19,625
And that preparation was through this false rumor that spread around on the battleground in Uhud(أحَد),

174
00:11:19,894 --> 00:11:21,758
 that Rasool Allah ﷺ has died

175
00:11:23,576 --> 00:11:25,054
and then the Ayah(آية) was revealed,

176
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:30,701
وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ ۚ أَفَإِنْ مَاتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلَىٰ أَعْقَابِكُمْ ۚ

177
00:11:31,447 --> 00:11:32,650
Muhammad(محمد) is a messenger,

178
00:11:32,754 --> 00:11:35,253
He is but a messenger and there have been many messengers before him

179
00:11:35,917 --> 00:11:41,795
so if he dies you shouldn't fall back on your heels and retreat

180
00:11:42,489 --> 00:11:45,987
you should carry on, forward with the message,

181
00:11:46,328 --> 00:11:49,550
so Allahعَزّوجَلّ prepared them through this Ghazwa(غزوة).

182
00:11:50,515 --> 00:11:53,684
So these are lessons from the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

183
00:11:55,012 --> 00:11:57,125
We'll talk about events between Al-Uhud(أحَد) and Al-Khandaq(اَلْخَنْدق).

184
00:11:57,656 --> 00:11:58,577
Number one;

185
00:11:58,737 --> 00:12:07,213
Rasool Allah ﷺ heard news that Bannu Asad(بنو اسد) are mobilizing forces to attack Madina

186
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:13,092
these are tribes in Najd(نجد) and they were headed by Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة الاسدي).

187
00:12:13,469 --> 00:12:16,458
And this man is this man is quite fascinating.

188
00:12:17,338 --> 00:12:22,283
His story is interesting, he started out by fighting against Rasool Allah ﷺ

189
00:12:22,770 --> 00:12:24,898
and then becoming Muslim after that

190
00:12:25,541 --> 00:12:27,683
and then after Rasool Allah ﷺ passes away,

191
00:12:27,795 --> 00:12:31,961
 he apostates and claims to be a prophet

192
00:12:32,941 --> 00:12:36,177
and then after that, he changes his mind and becomes a Muslim again

193
00:12:37,026 --> 00:12:39,002
and he fights Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

194
00:12:39,106 --> 00:12:41,107
That was the end of his life, he was Mujahid(مجاهد).

195
00:12:41,588 --> 00:12:46,938
So, he is kind of experienced it at all Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة الاسدي).

196
00:12:46,978 --> 00:12:50,082
Any way he was recruiting men to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ

197
00:12:50,657 --> 00:12:57,532
and Rasool Allah ﷺ as we said he would strike them, take them by surprise.

198
00:12:57,794 --> 00:13:01,974
So Rasool Allah ﷺ sent an army led by Abu Salama(ابوسلمه)

199
00:13:02,605 --> 00:13:05,949
and Abu Salama(ابوسلمه), by the way, was injured in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد)

200
00:13:06,418 --> 00:13:10,742
So he went out in this Sariyyah(سرية)

201
00:13:11,229 --> 00:13:16,393
and the enemy was defeated and he came back with a lot of cattle

202
00:13:17,147 --> 00:13:22,306
and but his injury, which was almost going to heal,

203
00:13:22,615 --> 00:13:28,236
now erupted again and he died, Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), this is Abu Salama(ابوسلمه).

204
00:13:28,617 --> 00:13:33,875
Another tribe was mobilizing, forced to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ

205
00:13:34,243 --> 00:13:35,425
and these were Hudail(هذيل),

206
00:13:35,979 --> 00:13:39,944
and their leader was Khalid Bin Sufiaan Al-Hudali( خالد بن سفيان الهذلي)

207
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,319
Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

208
00:13:43,918 --> 00:13:52,327
Khalid Bin Sufiaan Al-Hudali( خالد بن سفيان الهذلي) is recruiting an army to fight us.

209
00:13:53,247 --> 00:13:55,374
 So, go and kill him.

210
00:13:56,027 --> 00:14:00,483
These orders were delivered to Abdullah Bin Unais رضي الله عنه

211
00:14:00,994 --> 00:14:02,565
who was from the tribe of Juhainah(جهينة).

212
00:14:02,605 --> 00:14:08,129
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him that Hudail(هذيل) are gathering men,

213
00:14:08,478 --> 00:14:14,603
under the leadership of Khalid Bin Sufiaan Al-Hudali( خالد بن سفيان الهذلي), so go and kill him.

214
00:14:15,337 --> 00:14:19,134
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) said; Can you describe him for me,

215
00:14:19,410 --> 00:14:22,554
so that I will know him, I will recognize him, because he never saw him before.

216
00:14:22,981 --> 00:14:27,012
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, if you see him, you will tremble.

217
00:14:28,323 --> 00:14:33,968
This man Khalid Bin Sufiaan(خالد بن سفيان), if you see him you would tremble.

218
00:14:34,515 --> 00:14:41,705
Possibly that could be because this man Khalid Bin Sufiaan(خالد بن سفيان) was such a powerful figure

219
00:14:41,745 --> 00:14:44,047
 that whenever anybody who see him, he would tremble.

220
00:14:44,710 --> 00:14:49,469
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس), said I never trembled for the sight of anyone

221
00:14:49,863 --> 00:14:54,768
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him but if you see Khalid Bin Sufiaan(خالد بن سفيان), you would tremble.

222
00:14:55,085 --> 00:14:59,551
 So, this tells you that Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) was the right person to choose.

223
00:14:59,591 --> 00:15:04,273
He was a courageous man, he wasn't somebody who would fear others.

224
00:15:04,972 --> 00:15:09,005
So he said, I never trembled because of anyone.

225
00:15:09,510 --> 00:15:12,674
But this was going to be a special sign

226
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:17,432
in which, he would be able to recognize who is Khalid Bin Al-Hudail( خالد بن الهذلي)

227
00:15:17,763 --> 00:15:21,577
So, Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) said, I carried my sword, and I went out.

228
00:15:22,124 --> 00:15:26,698
And Rasool Allah ﷺ told him that he's gathering the men in Uranah(عرنة) in Arafaat(عرفات).

229
00:15:27,331 --> 00:15:33,298
So, he was gathering them close to Makkah, close to where his tribe lives.

230
00:15:33,525 --> 00:15:36,902
 And obviously, that territory is all supportive of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

231
00:15:37,594 --> 00:15:44,394
So, he is recruiting an army so he opens up a camp

232
00:15:44,809 --> 00:15:48,172
and he's recruiting men to that camp.

233
00:15:49,157 --> 00:15:57,565
Abdullah Bin Unais رضي الله عنه said, I was walking towards this man and when I saw him, I shivered.

234
00:15:58,260 --> 00:16:02,456
So, I knew that this man is Khalid Bin Sufiaan(خالد بن سفيان).

235
00:16:03,459 --> 00:16:08,695
And he was with some women trying to find a camp ground for them.

236
00:16:08,754 --> 00:16:13,786
 These were his women wives, daughters, sisters, whatever, women from his family.

237
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,985
So he was with them trying to find for them a camp.

238
00:16:18,445 --> 00:16:21,321
So, he walked towards him and he said it was time for Asar(عصر).

239
00:16:21,849 --> 00:16:28,470
And I was worried that my fight with him could preoccupy me from Salah(صلاة).

240
00:16:28,518 --> 00:16:30,948
 I mean Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) how long this fight will take.

241
00:16:31,425 --> 00:16:34,327
So, it could preoccupy me from Salah(صلاة), I could be killed.

242
00:16:34,725 --> 00:16:37,445
And since it is already time for Asr(عصر), I need to pray Asr(عصر),

243
00:16:37,487 --> 00:16:41,834
but the problem is, how can you pray Asr(عصر) in the presence of this man?

244
00:16:42,414 --> 00:16:44,826
I mean he would recognize that he's a Muslim.

245
00:16:45,322 --> 00:16:49,310
So, he said, I was praying while I was walking towards him

246
00:16:49,576 --> 00:16:53,864
and my Sujood(سجود) and Rukooh(ركوع) would be movement of my head.

247
00:16:54,447 --> 00:16:58,880
He would move his head, and that would be his Rukooh(ركوع) and Sujood(سجود).

248
00:16:59,895 --> 00:17:04,212
And he said, when I reached him, he said, and who is the man, who are you?

249
00:17:05,097 --> 00:17:14,376
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) said, I am a Bedouin Arab, who heard about your plans to fight Muhammad(محمد).

250
00:17:14,416 --> 00:17:15,654
So I came to join you.

251
00:17:15,979 --> 00:17:21,145
He said; yes, that is what I'm doing, I'm gathering forces to fight against Muhammadﷺ.

252
00:17:22,016 --> 00:17:25,183
So, Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) said I talked with him, for a while

253
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:28,408
until I felt confident that I can now attack

254
00:17:28,534 --> 00:17:30,671
and I attacked him with my sword and killed him.

255
00:17:31,419 --> 00:17:37,241
He said I left him with his women crouched over him, so he killed him.

256
00:17:37,281 --> 00:17:42,567
 It was laying on the ground and all of these women came swarming around the dead body.

257
00:17:42,797 --> 00:17:44,638
 And Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) left

258
00:17:45,074 --> 00:17:48,564
and he enters Madina Rasool Allah ﷺ saw him and said;

259
00:17:48,675 --> 00:17:49,880
اَفْلَحَ الْوَجْهْ

260
00:17:50,044 --> 00:17:53,911
 May this face succeed, he is making Dua(دعا) for Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس).

261
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,880
Abdullah(عبدالله) said: I killed him.

262
00:17:56,078 --> 00:17:57,854
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes, you did.

263
00:17:57,984 --> 00:17:59,333
 You are speaking the truth.

264
00:18:00,168 --> 00:18:04,093
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ calls him indoors, he calls him into his house

265
00:18:04,486 --> 00:18:06,392
and he gives him a stick.

266
00:18:07,571 --> 00:18:10,820
So, Abdullah Bin Unais رضي الله عنه takes the stick and leaves.

267
00:18:11,666 --> 00:18:12,943
His people met him and said,

268
00:18:13,122 --> 00:18:14,432
Why did Rasool Allah give you this stick.

269
00:18:14,472 --> 00:18:15,931
He said I don't know, he just gave it to me.

270
00:18:16,019 --> 00:18:17,263
They said go back and ask him.

271
00:18:17,493 --> 00:18:18,858
Why did they give you this stick?

272
00:18:19,593 --> 00:18:22,069
Abdullah Bin Unais رضي الله عنه said, I went back

273
00:18:22,109 --> 00:18:25,045
 and I asked Rasool Allah ﷺ, Why did you give me this stick.

274
00:18:25,502 --> 00:18:31,891
Rasool Allah ﷺ said this will be a sign between me and you, on the Day of Judgment.

275
00:18:33,010 --> 00:18:35,191
Abdullah Bin Unais رضي الله عنه said;

276
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:39,652
I tied that stick to my sword, meaning it was always with me

277
00:18:40,178 --> 00:18:45,005
and when he died, his instructions were to bury that stick with him

278
00:18:45,525 --> 00:18:49,291
And it was wrapped with him, in his shroud and buried with him.

279
00:18:49,905 --> 00:18:52,581
So that on the Day of Judgment, when he is resurrected

280
00:18:53,127 --> 00:18:57,906
he can have that stick as a sign between him and Rasool Allah ﷺ.

281
00:18:58,927 --> 00:19:00,860
And by the way, Rasool Allah ﷺ said in the Hadith(حديث).

282
00:19:01,317 --> 00:19:04,773
And on that day, a few people will have something to lean on.

283
00:19:05,645 --> 00:19:07,504
When he told him that I give you the stick

284
00:19:07,773 --> 00:19:10,153
to be a sign between me and you on the Day of Judgment.

285
00:19:10,481 --> 00:19:14,775
He also told him, And on that day few people will have something to lean on.

286
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:21,122
 The scholars say that this means few people will have deeds on which to lean on, on the Day of Judgment.

287
00:19:21,562 --> 00:19:26,932
And so, this is the story of the assassination of Khalid Bin Sufiaan Al-Hudali( خالد بن سفيان الهذلي).

288
00:19:27,406 --> 00:19:34,963
And due to his assassination that ended the plan of Hudail(هذيل) to attack Rasool Allah ﷺ.

289
00:19:35,076 --> 00:19:38,636
So, it shows you that Rasool Allah did not choose to fight the tribe of Hudail(هذيل)

290
00:19:39,283 --> 00:19:41,620
and rather he chose to assassinate Khalid(خالد),

291
00:19:41,913 --> 00:19:46,143
because the problem was with Khalid(خالد) and to spare the blood of the people.

292
00:19:46,172 --> 00:19:49,453
 Rasool Allah ﷺ assassinated this single man because

293
00:19:49,666 --> 00:19:53,000
some people might wonder, I mean, what are these political assassinations

294
00:19:53,054 --> 00:19:54,689
that Rasool Allah ﷺ was involved in?

295
00:19:54,872 --> 00:19:59,539
Well, that is to save the people from bloodshed rather than fighting the whole tribe

296
00:19:59,998 --> 00:20:04,689
who would not have otherwise fight with Rasool Allah ﷺ if it wasn't for Khalid Bin Hudail( خالد بن الهذيل).

297
00:20:04,902 --> 00:20:09,783
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to take care of this problem by reducing the bloodshed

298
00:20:09,845 --> 00:20:14,892
 and that is by killing this man, who is the cause of the whole problem.

299
00:20:16,094 --> 00:20:18,445
This was a man with an outstanding personality

300
00:20:18,470 --> 00:20:22,232
and ability to lead the people and he was leading them into evil.

301
00:20:22,468 --> 00:20:24,944
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ took him out of the way

302
00:20:25,223 --> 00:20:28,958
and that spared the Muslims and the people of Hudail(هذيل) from war.

303
00:20:30,013 --> 00:20:36,812
Rasool Allah ﷺ sends a group of 10 men for a mission and their leader was Asim Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه.

304
00:20:37,768 --> 00:20:41,354
They reach to the land of Bannu Lahyaan(بنو لحيان),

305
00:20:41,811 --> 00:20:44,821
and they are ambushed by 100 archers

306
00:20:45,084 --> 00:20:47,100
so 100 against 10.

307
00:20:47,793 --> 00:20:54,526
So, they fled to a small hill, they climb that hill or a rock,

308
00:20:55,313 --> 00:20:57,824
 and these hundred archers surrounded them.

309
00:20:58,866 --> 00:21:04,337
The archers told them come down, we guarantee you that we wouldn't kill you.

310
00:21:05,134 --> 00:21:08,457
We pledge that we wouldn't kill you, this is our word.

311
00:21:08,941 --> 00:21:10,207
The Ameer(امير) said;

312
00:21:10,502 --> 00:21:14,646
I do not accept the pledges of Mushrikeen(مشركين),

313
00:21:15,385 --> 00:21:18,346
I do not accept your word, I do not accept your pledge.

314
00:21:19,110 --> 00:21:22,062
And he chose to fight, this was the Ameer(امير), Asim Bin Thabit(عاصم بن ثابت).

315
00:21:22,650 --> 00:21:25,048
So they fight, seven get killed.

316
00:21:25,522 --> 00:21:28,531
So you have three remaining, they surrendered

317
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:31,621
and they were tied up in ropes.

318
00:21:32,533 --> 00:21:35,806
One of them felt that they would be betrayed

319
00:21:36,377 --> 00:21:40,998
and he was able to pull out his hand from the ropes

320
00:21:41,844 --> 00:21:50,832
and he drew out his sword and tried to attack these men from Bannu Lahyaan(بنو لحيان).

321
00:21:50,973 --> 00:21:56,234
But they kept a distance from him and kept on pelting him with rocks, until they killed him.

322
00:21:57,083 --> 00:22:02,731
 And they took the other two men and sold them to the people of Makkah.

323
00:22:03,287 --> 00:22:10,166
These two men Khabbab(خَبَّاب) and Zaid Bin (الدثنة)Dathinnah رضي الله عنهما.

324
00:22:11,162 --> 00:22:15,158
Now, obviously we would know what the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) would do with these two men,

325
00:22:15,198 --> 00:22:15,877
they would kill them.

326
00:22:16,476 --> 00:22:19,919
So, they decide that they're going to kill the two men.

327
00:22:20,588 --> 00:22:23,701
They take them out of Makkah because Makkah is Haram(حرم)

328
00:22:23,741 --> 00:22:25,019
 and you are not supposed to kill in Makkah.

329
00:22:25,045 --> 00:22:27,780
So they take them outside the boundaries of Makkah

330
00:22:28,719 --> 00:22:31,472
and they ask these two men

331
00:22:32,455 --> 00:22:38,987
they tell them would you wish that Muahmmad(محمد) is in your place and you are safe with your family.

332
00:22:39,490 --> 00:22:49,001
They respond by saying, we don't wish to be safe with our family while Muhammadﷺ is hurt by a thorn

333
00:22:49,542 --> 00:22:54,584
and we would rather die than Rasool Allah ﷺ being hurt.

334
00:22:55,033 --> 00:22:56,241
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) said;

335
00:22:56,394 --> 00:23:02,278
مَا رَاَيْتُ اَحَدًا يُحِبُّ اَحَدًا كَحُبِّ اَصْحَابْ مُحَمَّدِ مُحَمَّدًا

336
00:23:02,786 --> 00:23:06,583
I've never seen a people, who love their leader

337
00:23:07,069 --> 00:23:09,757
more than the people of Muahmmad(محمد), love him.

338
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:16,828
And I want to stop here and bring up this issue of loving Rasool Allah ﷺ.

339
00:23:17,488 --> 00:23:23,138
The love of the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ was so true and so deep

340
00:23:23,833 --> 00:23:28,427
that it was even known to the enemies of Muhammadﷺ.

341
00:23:29,979 --> 00:23:34,215
So, here you have Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) admitting, because it was so compelling,

342
00:23:34,837 --> 00:23:39,901
the evidence was so clear, the issue was so impressive

343
00:23:40,659 --> 00:23:49,719
that Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), the leader of the enemies of Rasool Allah ﷺ admits publicly

344
00:23:50,390 --> 00:23:56,101
and says, I've never seen people, who love someone like the Sahabah(صحابه) love Muhmmad(محمد).

345
00:23:57,322 --> 00:24:00,912
And this wasn't because, see,

346
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:04,796
if the Sahabah(صحابه) would claim that they love Muhammadﷺ day and night,

347
00:24:04,836 --> 00:24:06,364
 that wouldn't have made a difference.

348
00:24:06,824 --> 00:24:10,800
But the love of Muhammadﷺ emanated from their actions

349
00:24:11,570 --> 00:24:13,849
it was reflected in their deeds.

350
00:24:14,557 --> 00:24:16,898
Here you have two men facing death

351
00:24:17,422 --> 00:24:20,533
and they were asked whether you wish to be safe

352
00:24:20,629 --> 00:24:24,820
with your family, with your kids with your wife in the comfort of your home

353
00:24:25,465 --> 00:24:27,870
and have Muhammadﷺ here instead of you, they said,

354
00:24:28,086 --> 00:24:33,414
We would rather give our lives, than Muhammadﷺ be pricked by a thorn, be hurt by a thorn.

355
00:24:34,230 --> 00:24:40,034
So, this issue of loving Muhammadﷺ was so well known to everyone.

356
00:24:41,692 --> 00:24:47,094
They are both killed, as far as we know that, Khabbab(خَبَّاب), he was crucified.

357
00:24:48,148 --> 00:24:51,117
And his body remained on that cross

358
00:24:51,759 --> 00:24:57,593
until Ummayyah Bin Amr Adh-Dhamri(اُمَيَّةَ بن عَمْرُو اَلضَّمْرِيْ) comes and takes the body and buries it.

359
00:24:58,281 --> 00:25:04,475
Khabbab رضي الله عنه before his death, he asks this woman

360
00:25:04,545 --> 00:25:08,785
because he was held captive in the house of this woman, who lost her husband.

361
00:25:09,491 --> 00:25:11,629
And they said that

362
00:25:11,975 --> 00:25:15,009
it was Khabbab(خَبَّاب), who killed her husband in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

363
00:25:15,545 --> 00:25:18,586
So, it was this family that was going to take revenge.

364
00:25:18,969 --> 00:25:20,347
So he was in their house,

365
00:25:20,793 --> 00:25:24,151
so he tells this woman can you bring me a steel blade

366
00:25:24,728 --> 00:25:27,768
so that I can prepare myself for death.

367
00:25:27,808 --> 00:25:32,553
What he wants to do with this blade is, to shave his pubic hair.

368
00:25:32,871 --> 00:25:36,680
So, she sends him the blade with her child, young child.

369
00:25:37,542 --> 00:25:42,452
In one narration it says that she gave it to him but then the child crawled onto the lap of Khabbab(خَبَّاب)

370
00:25:42,492 --> 00:25:43,789
 anyway doesn't make a difference.

371
00:25:44,006 --> 00:25:48,156
The child ended up, in the hands in the lap of Khabbab(خَبَّاب)

372
00:25:49,351 --> 00:25:53,793
When the woman sees child in Khabbab(خَبَّاب)'s lap

373
00:25:54,563 --> 00:25:58,103
and he's holding this blade in his hand,

374
00:25:58,626 --> 00:26:00,182
what would she think?

375
00:26:00,861 --> 00:26:05,607
Khabbab(خَبَّاب) saw that she's worried that he might kill this child.

376
00:26:06,473 --> 00:26:07,378
But he told her;

377
00:26:07,418 --> 00:26:09,657
 مَا كُنْتُ لِاَفْعَلْ ذَالِكَ اِنْشَاءَ الله

378
00:26:09,697 --> 00:26:11,541
That's not something I would do.

379
00:26:12,202 --> 00:26:14,947
In Sha Allah(ان شاءالله), that's not going to be something that I would do

380
00:26:15,827 --> 00:26:17,825
And the lesson here to learn is that,

381
00:26:17,947 --> 00:26:26,689
even though he was going to be killed by the Kuffar(كفار) that didn't make him take revenge on a child, an innocent child.

382
00:26:27,355 --> 00:26:31,018
 And a Muslim is not a traitor, a Muslim would not betray

383
00:26:31,347 --> 00:26:35,782
and a Muslim would not take away the life of an innocent human being.

384
00:26:36,306 --> 00:26:40,340
 And even though he had a chance, and he already knew that he would be killed

385
00:26:40,826 --> 00:26:44,271
he could have taken revenge from that child, but he didn't.

386
00:26:45,140 --> 00:26:48,505
And that woman said, I've never seen a prisoner better than him

387
00:26:49,565 --> 00:26:54,310
I would come in and see him eating from a plate full of grapes,

388
00:26:54,556 --> 00:26:57,648
 when there are no grapes in Makkah whatsoever

389
00:26:58,310 --> 00:27:00,896
and I'm sure that he received those grapes from the angels.

390
00:27:01,150 --> 00:27:03,039
This is what a Mushrik(مشرك) woman, who was saying,

391
00:27:04,082 --> 00:27:04,726
Karamaat(كرامات).

392
00:27:05,353 --> 00:27:08,562
Now another lesson also is that, it shows you

393
00:27:08,846 --> 00:27:11,998
even though he was facing death, he still wanted to fulfill the Sunnah(سنة),

394
00:27:12,661 --> 00:27:15,897
he was going to shave his pubic hair, which is one of the Sunnan(سنن) of Fitrah(فطرة).

395
00:27:16,417 --> 00:27:17,922
He wanted to do that even though

396
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:23,545
you know, you could argue and say, well the Ummah(امة) has more important things to think about then shaving pubic hair.

397
00:27:23,585 --> 00:27:27,286
I mean let's get serious and start taking care of the important things.

398
00:27:27,326 --> 00:27:29,961
Well the Sahabah رضي الله عنه, they will take everything seriously.

399
00:27:30,001 --> 00:27:31,829
Everything in Islam was serious to them,

400
00:27:32,252 --> 00:27:37,755
so even though he's facing death, he still wants to follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

401
00:27:37,795 --> 00:27:44,308
Also before he was crucified, he sought permission from his crucifiers.

402
00:27:44,763 --> 00:27:46,412
He said, allow me to pray.

403
00:27:46,676 --> 00:27:49,435
So, they did grant him time to pray.

404
00:27:49,555 --> 00:27:50,840
 He prayed two Rak'ah(ركعة).

405
00:27:51,039 --> 00:27:53,059
When he finished he looked at them and said;

406
00:27:53,247 --> 00:27:58,806
If it wasn't for the fear of you, accusing me of being afraid of death,

407
00:27:58,846 --> 00:28:02,005
I would have making these two Rak'ah(ركعة) longer.

408
00:28:02,744 --> 00:28:07,141
So, he made the Salah(صلاة) short, so that they wouldn't think that he's afraid of dying.

409
00:28:07,957 --> 00:28:13,146
And he is the first one to start this Sunnah(سنة) of praying two Rak'ah(ركعة) before death.

410
00:28:13,430 --> 00:28:17,304
Later on, it became a Sunnah(سنة) because of his action.

411
00:28:19,236 --> 00:28:25,598
Khubaib رضي الله عنه was killed, and Zaid(زيد) was killed

412
00:28:25,832 --> 00:28:27,528
and Abdullah Bin Tariq(عبدالله بن طارق) was killed.

413
00:28:27,670 --> 00:28:31,720
So, now you have the entire group of 10 ended up dead, all of them.

414
00:28:32,347 --> 00:28:34,252
 Seven were killed on the spot

415
00:28:35,205 --> 00:28:37,796
Abdullah Bin Tariq(عبد الله بن طارق) was killed on the way to Makkah

416
00:28:38,142 --> 00:28:40,824
and the other two were killed in Makkah, so all of them were killed.

417
00:28:41,286 --> 00:28:44,942
The Munafiqeen(منافقين) what they said was and this is according to Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس)

418
00:28:45,798 --> 00:28:50,196
they said, How sad for those misguided people who died that way.

419
00:28:50,796 --> 00:28:55,425
They neither stayed with their families, nor did they carry out their masters mission.

420
00:28:56,675 --> 00:28:59,958
What the Munafiqeen(منافقين) are saying is that these 10 men are a failure.

421
00:29:00,702 --> 00:29:03,982
They ended up dying for nothing, the mission wasn't accomplished

422
00:29:04,691 --> 00:29:06,930
and they ended up losing their lives for nothing.

423
00:29:07,511 --> 00:29:09,708
If they stayed home, it would have been better for them.

424
00:29:11,030 --> 00:29:13,643
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية) saying,

425
00:29:14,303 --> 00:29:27,485
وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُعْجِبُكَ قَوْلُهُ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَيُشْهِدُ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا فِي قَلْبِهِ وَهُوَ أَلَدُّ الْخِصَامِ۝

426
00:29:28,826 --> 00:29:33,219
And of the people is, he whose speech pleases you in worldly life

427
00:29:33,762 --> 00:29:37,133
and he calls Allah to witness as to what is in his heart

428
00:29:37,581 --> 00:29:40,024
yet he is the fiercest of opponents.

429
00:29:40,315 --> 00:29:42,131
So, this Ayah(آية) is talking about the Munafiqeen(منافقين)

430
00:29:42,671 --> 00:29:43,791
and Allah says;

431
00:29:44,081 --> 00:29:56,620
وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَشْرِي نَفْسَهُ ابْتِغَاءَ مَرْضَاتِ اللَّهِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ رَءُوفٌ بِالْعِبَادِ۝

432
00:29:57,552 --> 00:30:02,934
And of the people is he, who sells himself seeking means to the approval of Allah

433
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:04,881
and Allah is kind to His servants

434
00:30:05,568 --> 00:30:07,779
And this is the Aayah(آية) talking about these 10 men

435
00:30:08,050 --> 00:30:10,674
that they sold themselves to Allah.

436
00:30:11,326 --> 00:30:13,623
It doesn't make a difference if they achieved the mission or not

437
00:30:13,764 --> 00:30:16,274
these men have given their lives for Allahعَزّوجَل.

438
00:30:16,314 --> 00:30:20,989
So, they will be credited for that and they will be rewarded by Allahعَزّوجَلّ greatly.

439
00:30:21,823 --> 00:30:25,791
 And what the Munafiqeen(منافقين) are saying could come in different forms.

440
00:30:25,835 --> 00:30:30,101
 I mean, they could have presented it in the form of these men don't have Hikmah(حكمه).

441
00:30:30,525 --> 00:30:34,650
If they had Hikmah(حكمه), they wouldn't have killed themselves in such a way.

442
00:30:35,002 --> 00:30:38,996
These men were, they were rash, and

443
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:43,131
they should not went out and taking this unnecessary risk.

444
00:30:43,219 --> 00:30:47,281
But all of these ways of saying it, are missing the important point here

445
00:30:47,321 --> 00:30:48,758
and that is what was your Niyyah(نية).

446
00:30:49,646 --> 00:30:51,528
The Niyyah(نية) of these men was right,

447
00:30:51,922 --> 00:30:54,143
therefore they died Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عَزُّوجَل).

448
00:30:55,011 --> 00:30:56,945
Whether the mission was accomplished or not,

449
00:30:57,136 --> 00:31:00,430
it doesn't affect the validity of that Niyyah(نية).

450
00:31:01,009 --> 00:31:03,267
The Niyyah(نية) was appropriate, the Niyyah(نية) was right

451
00:31:03,908 --> 00:31:07,446
and that is how Allahعَزّوجَلّ accepts the deed, from a person.

452
00:31:07,831 --> 00:31:12,123
Not every mission will be successful not every battle will be won.

453
00:31:12,332 --> 00:31:15,594
But Allahعَزّوجَلّ holds you accountable to your Niyyah(نية),

454
00:31:15,882 --> 00:31:16,963
what was the Niyyah(نية).?

455
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:26,099
Another event that occurred between the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) and Al-Khandaq(الخندق), is Bier Maoonah(بئر معونة).

456
00:31:27,108 --> 00:31:31,403
One of the leaders of the tribes of Najd(نجد) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said,

457
00:31:32,237 --> 00:31:36,733
Islam is spreading among my people, I want you to send me preachers

458
00:31:37,642 --> 00:31:39,506
who would call to Islam Dua'ah(دعوات).

459
00:31:40,290 --> 00:31:43,149
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ send over 70 men.

460
00:31:43,755 --> 00:31:47,023
These men were called the Al-Qur'rah(القرآء), the reciters of Qur'an.

461
00:31:47,391 --> 00:31:50,428
They would work during the day by selling wood

462
00:31:51,054 --> 00:31:55,952
and they would spend the night in the Qiyyaam Ul Lail(قيام اليل), in reciting Qur'an.

463
00:31:56,927 --> 00:31:58,130
This was their life.

464
00:31:58,217 --> 00:32:02,116
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ sends them over to teach these people about Islam.

465
00:32:02,141 --> 00:32:03,569
So they are Dua'ah(دعوات) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

466
00:32:04,170 --> 00:32:08,486
and they were given a guarantee of safety by this man, Abul Bara'a(ابو البرآء),

467
00:32:09,423 --> 00:32:10,930
who's called Mala'a Bin Athinna(ملاعب بن الاَسنة).

468
00:32:11,990 --> 00:32:14,249
When they reach to his territory.

469
00:32:14,963 --> 00:32:25,207
His nephew, Amir Bin Tufail(عامر بن طفيل) invites the men of his tribe to fight against the seventy Qur'a(قرآء).

470
00:32:25,778 --> 00:32:33,629
So, his uncle refuses, but he is successful in bringing up a force sufficient to attack these 70 men.

471
00:32:33,968 --> 00:32:37,564
Now this Amir Bin Tufail(عامر بن طفيل) has already met with Rasool Allah ﷺ previously

472
00:32:38,229 --> 00:32:43,310
and he told him;  O, Muahmmad(محمد), I give you three alternatives.

473
00:32:44,032 --> 00:32:53,365
Number one, you become king over the towns and I become king over the Bedouin people,

474
00:32:54,086 --> 00:32:56,749
as if this issue is all about kingdom.

475
00:32:57,348 --> 00:33:00,626
Number two you make me a Khalifah(خليفه), after you.

476
00:33:00,666 --> 00:33:03,157
You announced that when you die, I become king after you.

477
00:33:03,770 --> 00:33:06,534
Third choice if you refused, number one and two

478
00:33:06,863 --> 00:33:09,284
I'll attack you, with an army of 2000 men.

479
00:33:09,876 --> 00:33:15,740
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused obviously would not even talk to respond to us nonsense.

480
00:33:16,466 --> 00:33:17,551
So he was upset.

481
00:33:17,926 --> 00:33:21,351
This is one of the reasons, why he wanted to attack and kill these 70 men

482
00:33:22,163 --> 00:33:24,178
and they were massacred.

483
00:33:24,250 --> 00:33:27,922
These 70 men were massacred, a great disaster.

484
00:33:28,470 --> 00:33:30,440
When the news reached to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

485
00:33:30,480 --> 00:33:33,584
it was immediately conveyed, when the news was reached to Rasool Allah ﷺ

486
00:33:33,980 --> 00:33:37,102
Rasool Allah ﷺ was greatly affected by that news

487
00:33:37,633 --> 00:33:42,542
and was very sad about what happened and the betrayal of these people.

488
00:33:43,315 --> 00:33:46,206
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ starts making Dua Al-Qanoot(دعا القنوت)

489
00:33:46,326 --> 00:33:47,882
and Dua Al-Qanoot(دعا القنوت) was never done before.

490
00:33:48,310 --> 00:33:50,876
This was the first time Rasool Allah ﷺ does Dua Al-Qanoot(دعا القنوت)

491
00:33:50,901 --> 00:33:55,620
and he would do it in Fajr(فجر), Zhuhar(ظهر) Asar(عصر), Maghrib(مغرب) and Ish'a(عشاء) in every salah(صلاة)

492
00:33:55,853 --> 00:33:57,884
and he would make Dua(دعا) against those people

493
00:33:58,460 --> 00:34:02,593
against the Raql(ركل) and Zaqwaan(ذكوان) and Lahyaan(لحيان) and these tribes

494
00:34:02,633 --> 00:34:06,712
that betrayed the Muslims and kill them in such cold blood.

495
00:34:07,673 --> 00:34:11,056
Rasool Allah ﷺ would make this Dua(دعا) in his Salah(صلاة), in every Salah.

496
00:34:11,996 --> 00:34:16,335
 Now Haraam Bin Malhaan(حرام بن ملحان), who was the Ameer(امير) of the group,

497
00:34:16,966 --> 00:34:20,395
 when he was talking to Amir Bin Tufail(عامر بن طفيل).

498
00:34:20,883 --> 00:34:24,512
Amir Bin Tufail(عامر بن طفيل) gives signal to one of his men to go and kill him.

499
00:34:24,720 --> 00:34:29,440
So this man, his name is Jabbar(جبار), he sneaks from behind Haraam(حرام),

500
00:34:29,664 --> 00:34:32,000
and he stabs him with his spear in his back.

501
00:34:32,691 --> 00:34:36,067
And the blade comes out from the chest of Haraam(حرام).

502
00:34:36,344 --> 00:34:38,297
So, you can imagine Haraam(حرام) standing here

503
00:34:38,762 --> 00:34:42,676
and staring down and seeing this blade sticking out from his chest.

504
00:34:43,935 --> 00:34:46,885
What does he say? Oh, my God, I'm dead.

505
00:34:47,736 --> 00:34:52,332
Oh, no, look what happened to me I'm worried about my kids.

506
00:34:52,980 --> 00:34:54,127
What does he say?

507
00:34:54,527 --> 00:34:57,546
His response was shocking to those present

508
00:34:58,333 --> 00:34:58,780
He said;

509
00:34:58,860 --> 00:35:02,410
 الله اكبر فُزْتُ وَرَبُّ الْكَعْبَه

510
00:35:03,018 --> 00:35:05,962
Allah is great, I have won,

511
00:35:06,434 --> 00:35:09,798
I have succeeded in the name of the Lord of Ka'aba(كعبه),

512
00:35:11,053 --> 00:35:12,083
I've succeeded.

513
00:35:12,689 --> 00:35:17,437
 That is what he said before he falls down as a Shaheed(شهيد).

514
00:35:18,306 --> 00:35:20,781
 Now, this was a shocking statement to make.

515
00:35:20,821 --> 00:35:27,073
 I mean man, you're suffering out of that pain, and your blood is gushing out of your wound.

516
00:35:27,113 --> 00:35:30,164
It says another narration that his hands were soaked in blood.

517
00:35:30,361 --> 00:35:33,113
And he takes the blood and he wipes it on his head and his face.

518
00:35:33,153 --> 00:35:36,773
And he says, I've succeeded in the name of Allah

519
00:35:37,850 --> 00:35:40,323
The man who killed him, would later on say

520
00:35:41,012 --> 00:35:44,017
when he's telling the story of how he became Muslim, he said;

521
00:35:44,679 --> 00:35:49,391
I stabbed the man from behind and spear came out from his chest.

522
00:35:49,953 --> 00:35:55,591
And he said, Allah is great, I have succeeded by the name of the Lord of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

523
00:35:55,898 --> 00:35:58,566
So, I went around asking, What is he talking about?

524
00:35:58,627 --> 00:35:59,714
What do you mean, you succeeded?

525
00:35:59,754 --> 00:36:01,959
I killed you, he's dead.

526
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:04,554
How can you say that he succeeded?

527
00:36:04,881 --> 00:36:07,101
They told him, he's talking about Shahadah(شهادة).

528
00:36:07,457 --> 00:36:08,979
He is talking about becoming a martyr.

529
00:36:09,446 --> 00:36:13,479
He has succeeded, he has succeeded in becoming a Shaheed(شهيد)

530
00:36:13,911 --> 00:36:16,559
and then they explain to him what Shaheed(شهيد) means.

531
00:36:16,875 --> 00:36:18,475
He said, and that's when I became Muslim.

532
00:36:18,515 --> 00:36:20,957
I said, Man, he has truly won, yes, he did!

533
00:36:21,745 --> 00:36:22,865
نَعْمْ لَقَدْ اَفْلَحْ

534
00:36:24,127 --> 00:36:27,934
When he understood where this Muslim is coming from,

535
00:36:28,588 --> 00:36:31,862
when he understood, what the concept of Shahadah(شهادة) is, he said, yes,

536
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:35,829
that makes sense now, he did succeed, and he became Muslim.

537
00:36:36,344 --> 00:36:37,713
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), you know,

538
00:36:38,251 --> 00:36:40,537
Haraam Bin Malhaan(حرام ابن ملحان) dies as a Shaheed(شهيد)

539
00:36:40,577 --> 00:36:45,174
and he also is giving Da'wah(دعوة), in his Shahadah(شهاده) and somebody is becomes Muslim because of that.

540
00:36:45,980 --> 00:36:49,067
His own assassin, becomes Muslim,

541
00:36:49,702 --> 00:36:52,897
because of those last words of Haraam Bin Malhaan(حرام بن ملحان),

542
00:36:52,937 --> 00:36:56,782
so not only is he a Shaheed(شهيد), but he's also a Daiyah(داعية), even in his last moments.

543
00:36:57,763 --> 00:37:02,273
That's the Barakah(بركة) that Allahعَزّوجَلّ has given to Haraam رضي الله عنه,

544
00:37:02,616 --> 00:37:06,099
I mean, you never know what's gonna bring people closer to Islam.

545
00:37:06,139 --> 00:37:10,154
I mean, who would have imagined that the statement made by Haraam(حرام)

546
00:37:10,194 --> 00:37:13,081
would actually be the reason for somebody becoming Muslim.

547
00:37:14,403 --> 00:37:16,945
Amir Bin Fuhairah(عامر بن فهيره), was one of these men

548
00:37:17,249 --> 00:37:19,320
You might remember the name of Aamir(عامر) from Hijrah(هجره).

549
00:37:19,360 --> 00:37:21,430
He was the servant of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

550
00:37:21,470 --> 00:37:24,222
He also accompanied them in the journey of Hijrah(هجرة).

551
00:37:25,101 --> 00:37:29,226
He was also the shepherd, who would bring the goats to the cave,

552
00:37:29,266 --> 00:37:31,597
 when Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) were in hiding.

553
00:37:31,902 --> 00:37:34,939
So, Aamir(عامر) was one of these 70 men and he was killed.

554
00:37:35,679 --> 00:37:40,367
By the way, I should have mentioned that only one of the 70 men,  his life was spared

555
00:37:40,407 --> 00:37:42,892
 and that is Amr Bin Ummayyah Adh-Dhamri(عمرو بن امية الضمري).

556
00:37:43,069 --> 00:37:46,630
They captured him, and he was freed

557
00:37:47,023 --> 00:37:50,667
because, when Amir Bin Tufail(عامر بن طفيل) knew that he is from Mudhar(مضر).

558
00:37:51,642 --> 00:37:54,011
The mother of Aamir(عامر) had made an oath that

559
00:37:54,035 --> 00:37:56,566
she is going to free a man from Mudhar(مضر).

560
00:37:56,853 --> 00:37:59,570
So, Aamir(عامر) said since this man is from Mudhar(مضر), we're going to free him

561
00:38:00,225 --> 00:38:02,903
and that would fulfill the oath of my mother.

562
00:38:02,968 --> 00:38:03,682
So, he was freed.

563
00:38:03,956 --> 00:38:08,849
Aamir(عامر) said, when they captured me, they pointed out to me

564
00:38:09,337 --> 00:38:12,009
a dead body of one of the 70 men

565
00:38:12,049 --> 00:38:13,654
and they said whose body is this?

566
00:38:13,694 --> 00:38:15,884
I told them, this is the body of Amir Bin Fuhairah(عامر بن فهيره).

567
00:38:16,254 --> 00:38:22,690
They said, when he was killed his body, went up in the sky and then came down.

568
00:38:23,653 --> 00:38:26,236
His body rose up in the sky

569
00:38:26,647 --> 00:38:30,682
and stayed there for a while and then it came down the angels sort of lifted him up.

570
00:38:31,838 --> 00:38:35,122
So, that's a Karamah(كرمة) that happened with Amir Bin Fuhairah(عامر بن فهيره).

571
00:38:36,049 --> 00:38:39,713
Forgot to mention something about Asim Bin Thabit(عاصم بن ثابت),

572
00:38:39,833 --> 00:38:43,260
Asim Bin Thabit(عاصم بن ثابت) go back to Rajiah(رجيعة),

573
00:38:43,822 --> 00:38:46,737
Asim Bin Thabit(عاصم بن ثابت) before he was killed.

574
00:38:46,780 --> 00:38:49,536
He said; See because he refused to give up.

575
00:38:49,576 --> 00:38:51,814
 He said I'm not gonna take the pledge from Kuffar(كفار).

576
00:38:52,659 --> 00:38:54,504
When they were killing his men,

577
00:38:55,348 --> 00:38:59,726
they were stripping them naked, they would take everything off them.

578
00:39:00,681 --> 00:39:03,110
So, Asim(عاصم), said: O Allah

579
00:39:03,593 --> 00:39:07,400
as I fought for your religion when I'm alive, protect my body when I'm dead.

580
00:39:07,822 --> 00:39:12,354
He didn't want them to strip him like they would do with the rest of his men.

581
00:39:12,750 --> 00:39:14,544
So, he made that Dua(دعا) to Allahعَزّوجَلّ

582
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:18,313
when he died they wanted to come and strip him.

583
00:39:18,353 --> 00:39:21,687
 In addition to that they also wanted to cut off his head because

584
00:39:22,210 --> 00:39:27,025
there was a woman whose sons were killed by Asim Bin Thabit(عاصم بن ثابت).

585
00:39:27,413 --> 00:39:35,496
So, she made an oath that if someone would bring her, the skull of Asim Bin Thabit(عاصم بن ثابت)

586
00:39:36,073 --> 00:39:38,478
she would pay him 100 camels

587
00:39:39,322 --> 00:39:41,914
and she would drink wine in his skull.

588
00:39:42,409 --> 00:39:46,556
So, these men knew that the skull of this man is worth 100 camels,

589
00:39:46,621 --> 00:39:48,619
 so they really want wanted to get it.

590
00:39:49,081 --> 00:39:55,220
Allahعَزّوجَلّ sends a swarm of wasps to protect the body of Asim(عاصم)

591
00:39:55,260 --> 00:39:59,844
 and whenever somebody would come close to him the wasp would jump on him and sting him.

592
00:40:00,292 --> 00:40:04,704
 So, they said let's leave him and come and claim his body tomorrow.

593
00:40:05,310 --> 00:40:09,031
At night Allahعَزّوجَلّ sends a flood that takes the body away

594
00:40:09,327 --> 00:40:11,544
and the body disappears and they couldn't find him.

595
00:40:12,489 --> 00:40:16,907
So, this is a Karamah(كرامة) that happened with Asim Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه.

596
00:40:17,176 --> 00:40:18,636
We'll carry on in Sha Allah ho Ta'ala(اِنْ شَاء الله تعالى),

597
00:40:18,676 --> 00:40:22,484
with some other events that happened between Uhud(أحَد) and Al-Khandaq(اَلْخَنْدق) tomorrow.

598
00:40:22,785 --> 00:40:26,846
رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ

599
00:40:26,886 --> 00:40:31,081
 وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

600
00:40:31,206 --> 00:40:33,260
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

